# Public SSH keys that may sign a release tag (v*). One key per line:
#
#   <principal> namespaces="git" <key type> <public key>
#
# for example
#
#   maintainer@example.org namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# The principal is a name for the signer, usually the address the tag is made
# with. The rest is the content of the signer's public key file (~/.ssh/<name>.pub).
# Only public keys belong here. Never put a private key in this file.
#
# .github/workflows/release.yml reads this file from the main branch, not from
# the tagged commit, and runs tools/verify_release_tag.py with it before it
# builds anything. While no key is listed, every release job fails.
# How to sign a tag: CONTRIBUTING.md, "Release tags".
